{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggp89Dmj5mB9bLAHaopZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I get **Dq ≈ 1702 cm⁻¹** and **B ≈ 639 cm⁻¹**. I solved this by hand with the standard d² strong-field matrix and did not use any of the session's tools.\n\n**Band assignment** (octahedral d², ground term ³T₁g(F)):\n- ν₁ = 15 730 cm⁻¹: ³T₁g(F) → ³T₂g\n- ν₂ = 24 030 cm⁻¹: ³T₁g(F) → ³T₁g(P)\n- ν₃ = 32 750 cm⁻¹: ³T₁g(F) → ³A₂g\n\n**Energy expressions**\n\nThe two ³T₁g states mix through the 2×2 matrix [[−8Dq − 5B, 6B], [6B, 2Dq + 4B]]. Diagonalising it and taking each energy relative to the ground state gives, with R = √(100Dq² + 180DqB + 225B²):\n\n- ν₁ = 5Dq − 7.5B + ½R\n- ν₂ = R\n- ν₃ = 15Dq − 7.5B + ½R\n\n**Solving**\n\n1. Subtracting ν₁ from ν₃ removes B and R: ν₃ − ν₁ = 10Dq = 32 750 − 15 730 = 17 020 cm⁻¹. So **Dq = 1702 cm⁻¹**.\n2. ν₂ gives R directly: R = 24 030 cm⁻¹.\n3. Putting both into ν₁: 15 730 = 8 510 − 7.5B + 12 015. This gives 7.5B = 4 795, so **B ≈ 639 cm⁻¹**.\n\n**Check:** with Dq = 1702 and B = 639.3, R = √(2.8968×10⁸ + 1.9586×10⁸ + 0.9196×10⁸) ≈ 24 031 cm⁻¹. That matches ν₂, so the three bands fit together consistently.\n\nThese are quartet-free triplet-to-triplet transitions, so they depend only on Dq and B. The Racah parameter C cannot be determined from these data; it would need spin-forbidden (singlet) bands.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1702, \"B\": 639, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Three spin-allowed d2 bands give 10Dq = ν3 − ν1 and B from the T1g(F)/T1g(P) mixing; C is undetermined.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7985,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7985,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_m